<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>The Modality Load of Different Layer Experts</h3>

<figure id="A3.F5" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2506.21864v1/assets/token_load_13.png" id="A3.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:381/197;" width="381" height="197" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 5: </span>The modality load of the experts in the middle layers.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A3.F6" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2506.21864v1/assets/token_load_26.png" id="A3.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:381/197;" width="381" height="197" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6: </span>The modality load of the experts in the last layers.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The expert load across different layers is illustrated in Figures <a href="#A3.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ C.2 The Modality Load of Different Layer Experts ‣ Appendix C Ablation Study ‣ DeepTalk: Towards Seamless and Smart Speech Interaction with Adaptive Modality-Specific MoE" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> and <a href="#A3.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ C.2 The Modality Load of Different Layer Experts ‣ Appendix C Ablation Study ‣ DeepTalk: Towards Seamless and Smart Speech Interaction with Adaptive Modality-Specific MoE" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, representing the modality load of an intermediate MoE layer and the final MoE layer, respectively. It is evident that there are significant differences in modality load across different layers. This indicates that the indices of audio experts in each layer are not the same.</p>
</div>
</section>
